From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:21:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] feat(ui): a phone reviews: one finger pans, a long hold
 for menus, no editing

A phone in the reviewer layout (FULL_UI off, <= 900px) is for reading and
answering a design, and three things got in the way.

Panning. A finger on a frame in the Comment tool did not pan: it went to the
frame and commented. Now a touch pans in the Hand and in Comment alike, and
a comment is a tap (the finger lifts within 6 px, no pinch, no hold).

The page zoomed. A pinch that landed outside the canvas's own handling, or a
double tap, zoomed the whole page, chrome and all. On phones the editor adds
maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no to the viewport tag while it is mounted,
cancels WebKit's gesturestart/gesturechange, and sets touch-action:
manipulation on its root, which is what tldraw and Excalidraw do. The canvas
pinch still zooms the canvas.

Menus opened by accident. Radix's context menu opens on a 700 ms touch press
and only cancels it on a move over the trigger itself. The stage captures the
pointer for a pan, so the frame never saw the finger move and its menu opened
mid-pan; a finger resting while reading opened it too. The Radix timer is
replaced (useTouchHold, src/lib/touchHold.ts): a hold opens the menu after
1600 ms, well past the platforms' own ~500 ms long press, and ends when the
finger lifts, drifts more than 10 px (tracked on window, so a captured pan
counts) or a second finger lands. The browser's own long-press contextmenu
is turned away. The finger that opened a menu holds the pan still until it
lifts. The mouse and right-click are unchanged.

No editing. A phone's role counts as review at most (roleOf caps edit at
review while store.reviewOnly is set; grantedRole is what the server gave,
so the access banner does not call it view-only). Every edit control that
gates on canEditOpenCanvas steps aside: the frame menu keeps Copy link,
export and the verdicts, drops Duplicate and Delete. The dock holds the Hand
and Comment and no tool list, setTool refuses the others, and Prototype mode
is off. Nothing here is a permission: the server's role is untouched, and a
wider window gets the full editor back.

Tests: tests/phoneReviewBrowser.test.ts (390x844 touch): the cap, the
viewport tag, a 1.2 s moving drag pans with no menu, no menu at 1000 ms and
one after the hold with its review items only, Comment pans and a tap
selects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
